{"study_id": "zk26_seeded_fold2_v3_haiku55_repeat2_20261106", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "1dad8049af47f222f73f6b488e20d7c1530e0e7c37c907f31aeb093fab05a924", "expression": "TS_CORR(RETURN($adj_close, 1.0), $volume, 48.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "TS_CORR", "args": [{"op": "RETURN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "volume"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 48.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Over the last 48 native 5m bars, the correlation between 5m simple returns and 5m volume measures whether recent price moves are coupled to traded volume. When the coupling is strongly positive, the trailing 12-bar move reflects sustained informed or forced flow and should persist over the next 12 bars. When coupling is weak or negative, the move is more likely thin-liquidity noise and should weaken or partly reverse. The primary tests MULTIPLY(TS_CORR(RETURN(adj_close,1), volume, 48), RETURN(adj_close,12)) against the target, with Control A (coupling alone) and Control B (trailing move alone) on identical rows. This is the intraday-span version of the daily coupling test in trial:189, which failed the quality gate.", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 246, "attempt": 246, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-27dcf84074"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_seeded_fold2_v3_haiku55_repeat2_20261106", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "12ceafba21a6f9ab4168181685d3ae711b193d1c5b138383ff36033160814ca1", "expression": "MULTIPLY(RETURN($adj_close, 12.0), TS_CORR(RETURN($adj_close, 12.0), DELAY(RETURN($adj_close, 12.0), 12.0), 240.0))", "canonical_expression": {"op": "MULTIPLY", "args": [{"op": "RETURN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 12.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "TS_CORR", "args": [{"op": "RETURN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 12.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "DELAY", "args": [{"op": "RETURN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 12.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 12.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 240.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}, "description": "Hourly-block serial dependence sets whether the last 12-bar (one-hour) adj_close log-return continues or reverses over the next 12 bars. The factor is the last 12-bar return multiplied by the rolling correlation, over 240 base bars, between 12-bar returns and their 12-bar lag, so each pair compares adjacent non-overlapping hourly blocks. Positive dependence predicts continuation, which means a positive raw IC. Stable negative raw IC is recorded as hourly reversal under negative dependence, a different account, and is not a pass.", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 260, "attempt": 260, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-27dcf84074"}]}
